# <type>[(<scope>)]: <description>
#   │                   │ 
#   │                   └─ imperative, present tense;
#   └─ see types below     no period; max ~72 chars
#
# [body]
#
# [footer(s)]
#
# =======================================================================
#
# Types:
#
# feat      -> new feature
# fix       -> bug fix
# docs      -> documentation only
# style     -> formatting (no logic change)
# refactor  -> code change that is neither a fix nor a feature
# perf      -> performance improvement
# test      -> adding or updating tests
# build     -> build system or dependencies
# ci        -> CI/CD changes
# chore     -> other (maintenance, tooling, cleanup)
# revert    -> revert previous commit
#
# Append '!' after type/scope to signal a breaking change:
#   feat(api)!: remove deprecated endpoint
#
# ======================================================================
#
# Optional body: (describe 'what' changed and 'why' -> not 'how')
#
# - explain the context or problem
# - describe reasoning behind the change
# - mention alternatives considered, if relevant
# - wrap at 72 chars
#
# ======================================================================
#
# Optional footer(s):
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# Closes: #123
# Fixes: #456
# Refs: #789
#
# More information on: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
